from ./Factory import Factory

export anchor FactoryGuide:
    howToRead:
        Read this specification as a sequence rather than as one flat list of
        requirements. Follow a link only when the work touches what it
        describes. The order below moves from why a project owns its factory,
        through how work is organized and executed, to delivery, capacity,
        surfaces, and the guarantees that hold them together.
    readingOrder:
        - @{Factory.referenceImplementation}
        - @{Factory.adoptionMapping}
        - @{Factory.adoptionConformance}
        - @{Factory.projectSpecificRealization}
        - @{Factory.incrementalAdoptionAndEvolution}
        - @{Factory.reviewSchedule}
        - @{Factory.proposalRecord}
        - @{Factory.approvalBoundary}
        - @{Factory.routingEvidence}
        - @{Factory.states}
        - @{Factory.factModel}
        - @{Factory.freshness}
        - @{Factory.healthScopes}
        - @{Factory.readAccess}
        - @{Factory.actionSet}
        - @{Factory.authorizationMatrix}
        - @{Factory.actorIdentity}
        - @{Factory.auditIntegrity}
        - @{Factory.decisionSet}
        - @{Factory.credentialBoundary}
        - @{Factory.configurationChanges}
        - @{Factory.orchestration}
        - @{Factory.planningAndExecution}
        - @{Factory.dependencies}
        - @{Factory.orderStates}
        - @{Factory.questions}
        - @{Factory.liveness}
        - @{Factory.harnessRecoveryMatrix}
        - @{Factory.retries}
        - @{Factory.priority}
        - @{Factory.jobs}
        - @{Factory.completionAssessment}
        - @{Factory.delivery}
        - @{Factory.deliveryTargets}
        - @{Factory.targetLeaseLifecycle}
        - @{Factory.overlapLeaseLifecycle}
        - @{Factory.leaseConformance}
        - @{Factory.integrationCandidates}
        - @{Factory.deliveryOutcomes}
        - @{Factory.partialDelivery}
        - @{Factory.deliveryMatrix}
        - @{Factory.workspaceIsolation}
        - @{Factory.budgetReservation}
        - @{Factory.accountingModel}
        - @{Factory.usageAttribution}
        - @{Factory.throttlingClassification}
        - @{Factory.adaptiveModelSelection}
        - @{Factory.standardSurface}
        - @{Factory.descriptorSchema}
        - @{Factory.conformanceScenarios}
        - @{Factory.conformanceReport}
        - @{Factory.conformanceIndependence}
        - @{Factory.conformanceVerdicts}
        - @{Factory.verifierIdentity}
        - @{Factory.reportAdmissibility}
        - @{Factory.verificationConformance}
        - @{Factory.budgetConformance}
        - @{Factory.durability}
        - @{Factory.recoveryInventory}
        - @{Factory.unresolvedRecovery}
        - @{Factory.retryRecovery}
        - @{Factory.recoveryMatrix}
        - @{Factory.artifactStore}
        - @{Factory.wiringKey}
    narrative:
        The first links explain why consuming projects own their factory and
        how it grows without a shared service. The plan, lifecycle, and
        execution links describe how an order becomes work and how that work
        survives failure. Delivery and workspace links describe how results
        become accepted changes. Capacity and routing links describe how the
        factory spends its available agents and money. Tooling and conformance
        links describe how an engineer and a verifying agent operate and trust
        the result. Persistence, evidence, and wiring links describe the
        guarantees underneath every other section.
